      "id": 26,
      "title": "Inference",
      "description": "Workers blocked on input is the autobatching signal: sustained above zero means the GPU is starved and the bottleneck is upstream of the model. Mean batch latency is derived from the cumulative counters rather than read directly, so it tracks the current window instead of the process lifetime.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 49
